    "id": "train-1339",
    "question": "A plumber bought 10 meters of copper and 5 more meters of plastic pipe. If each meter cost $4, how much did the plumber spent on the copper and plastic pipe?",
    "gold": "100",
    "answer": "He bought 10 + 5 = <<10+5=15>>15 meters of plastic pipe.\nThe total meters of the copper and plastic pipe is 10 + 15 = <<10+15=25>>25.\nThe plumber spent $4 x 25 = $<<4*25=100>>100 on copper and plastic pipe.\n#### 100"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total cost of the copper and plastic pipe that the plumber bought, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total length of the plastic pipe.\n2. Determine the cost of the copper pipe.\n3. Determine the cost of the plastic pipe.\n4. Add the costs of the copper and plastic pipes to find the total amount spent.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total length of the plastic pipe.\nThe plumber bought 5 more meters of plastic pipe than copper pipe. Since he bought 10 meters of copper pipe, the length of the plastic pipe is:\n\\[ 10 + 5 = 15 \\text{ meters} \\]\n\nStep 2: Determine the cost of the copper pipe.\nThe cost of each meter of copper pipe is $4. Therefore, the cost of 10 meters of copper pipe is:\n\\[ 10 \\times 4 = 40 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nStep 3: Determine the cost of the plastic pipe.\nThe cost of each meter of plastic pipe is $4. Therefore, the cost of 15 meters of plastic pipe is:\n\\[ 15 \\times 4 = 60 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nStep 4: Add the costs of the copper and plastic pipes to find the total amount spent.\nThe total amount spent is the sum of the cost of the copper pipe and the cost of the plastic pipe:\n\\[ 40 + 60 = 100 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nThus, the plumber spent \\(\\boxed{100}\\) dollars on the copper and plastic pipe.",
